| Using `||` for defaults (`info.name || 'x'`) | Treats falsy values like `0` or `''` as missing | Use `??` (nullish coalescing) instead |
| Forgetting to check `e` itself (e.g., when you call the handler manually) | `e` is `undefined` → `e.features` throws | Always start with `e?.` |

