## 4. Automatic fallback when an icon is missing

If you have a layer that may reference many different icon names (e.g. a POI layer where each feature has a `category` property) you can **listen for the “error” event** that MapLibre emits when it can’t find an image, then load it on‑the‑fly.

```js
// Keep a Set of icons we have already tried to load (to avoid loops)
const pendingIcons = new Set();

map.on('error', e => {
  // MapLibre wraps errors in an object with a `error` property
  const err = e?.error?.message || '';
  const match = err.match(/Image "([^"]+)" does not exist in the style sprite/);
  if (!match) return; // not an image‑missing error

  const missingName = match[1];
  if (pendingIcons.has(missingName)) return; // already loading / failed
  pendingIcons.add(missingName);

  // -------------------------------------------------
  // 1️⃣ Decide *where* to fetch the icon from.
  //    Here we assume a convention: `${name}.png` lives on a CDN.
  // -------------------------------------------------
  const url = `https://my-cdn.example.com/icons/${missingName}.png`;

  map.loadImage(url, (err, img) => {
    if (err) {
      console.warn(`⚠️ Could not load fallback icon "${missingName}" from ${url}`);
      pendingIcons.delete(missingName);
      return;
    }
    map.addImage(missingName, img);
    console.info(`✅ Dynamically added icon "${missingName}"`);
    // The layer will instantly re‑render with the new image.
  });
});
```

**Why this works**

* The error event fires *after* the style has been parsed but *before* the frame is drawn, so adding the image in the callback is fast enough for the same render cycle.
* By keeping a `Set` you avoid an infinite loop if the image truly does not exist on your server.

---

## 5. Dealing with **style changes** (`map.setStyle`)

When you call `map.setStyle(...)` the whole image registry is cleared.  
If you rely on dynamic icons you must **re‑register them after each style load**.

```js
// Store a list of icons you want to keep around
const dynamicIcons = [
  { name: 'my‑dynamic‑icon', url: 'https://example.com/icon.svg' },
  // …more
];

function registerDynamicIcons() {
  dynamicIcons.forEach(({name, url}) => {
    // Avoid duplicate registration errors
    if (map.hasImage(name)) return;
    map.loadImage(url, (err, img) => {
      if (!err) map.addImage(name, img);
    });
  });
}

// After any style change
map.on('styledata', () => {
  // `styledata` fires both on the initial load and on subsequent setStyle calls
  registerDynamicIcons();
});
```

