## 6. Advanced options you may need

| Option | What it does | When to use |
|--------|--------------|-------------|
| `sdf: true` | Treat the image as a **signed‑distance‑field** (allows color tinting via `icon-color`). | Use with Maki icons or any monochrome SVG you want to recolor on the fly. |
| `pixelRatio: 2` | Register a high‑DPI version of the image. | For retina displays; otherwise MapLibre will auto‑scale. |
| `stretchX` / `stretchY` | Define stretchable regions (9‑slice scaling). | When you need a resizable “badge” background. |
| `content` (for `image` source type) | Not needed for `addImage`, but useful if you want to treat the image as a *source* (e.g., a static raster overlay). | Rare, but possible. |

