## 4. Gotchas & Best Practices

| Issue | What to watch out for | Recommended fix |
|-------|----------------------|-----------------|
| **Retina / high‑DPI** | `addImage` defaults to `pixelRatio = 1`. On a device with `devicePixelRatio = 2` the icon will look blurry. | Pass `{pixelRatio: window.devicePixelRatio}` when you add the image, **or** generate a double‑size canvas and let MapLibre downscale. |
| **SDF vs. bitmap** | Only SDF images respect `icon-color`, `icon-halo-color`, etc. | If you need runtime colour changes, generate an SDF (e.g. via `tiny-sdf` or by pre‑exporting an SDF PNG) and set `{sdf: true}`. |
| **Memory** | Adding thousands of unique icons can blow GPU memory. | Cache generated images yourself (`const cache = new Map();`) and reuse them. Remove rarely‑used images with `map.removeImage(name)` if you know they won’t be needed again. |
| **Async race conditions** | Two layers may request the same missing name almost simultaneously, causing two fetches. | Guard with a `Promise` cache: `pendingPromises[id] = pendingPromises[id] ?? loadAndAdd(id);` |
| **Cross‑origin** | Remote PNGs from another domain need CORS headers (`Access‑Control‑Allow‑Origin:*`). | Either host icons on the same origin or enable CORS on the image server. |
| **Sprite fallback** | If you *do* have a sprite sheet, you can still let the event fire for names that are truly missing. | Keep the sprite as the primary source (fast, batched) and only fall back to `styleimagemissing` for the few dynamic ones. |

