Below is a complete, ready‑to‑copy recipe for dealing with **missing icons** that a MapLibre GL JS style asks for.  
It uses the **MapLibre event system** so you don’t have to edit the style JSON manually – the map will automatically fetch (or synthesize) the missing image the first time it is needed, and then keep it in the style’s image cache for the rest of the session.

---

## 1. Why the problem happens

When a style contains a `symbol` layer that references an image that has **not** been added to the map’s style image registry, MapLibre throws an error like:

```
Error: Image "my‑missing‑icon" not found.
```

In MapLibre GL JS (and in the upstream Mapbox GL JS) this situation is exposed as a **`styleimagemissing`** event.  
If you listen for that event you can:

1. **Detect** which image id is missing (`e.id`).
2. **Load** the image from wherever you keep your assets (static folder, CDN, data‑URI, generated canvas, etc.).
3. **Add** the image to the map (`map.addImage(e.id, image)`).
4. Optionally **fallback** to a placeholder if the real asset can’t be fetched.

Because the event fires **once per missing id**, you can safely add the same image multiple times – MapLibre will ignore duplicate `addImage` calls.

---

## 2. Minimal working example

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <title>MapLibre – graceful missing‑icon handling</title>
  <script src="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@4.2.0/dist/maplibre-gl.js"></script>
  <link href="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@4.2.0/dist/maplibre-gl.css" rel="stylesheet" />
  <style>
    body, html { margin:0; padding:0; height:100%; }
    #map { width:100%; height:100%; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="map"></div>

<script>
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  // 1️⃣  Initialise the map (any style that references an unknown icon)
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  const map = new maplibregl.Map({
    container: 'map',
    style: {
      version: 8,
      sources: {
        osm: {
          type: 'raster',
          tiles: ['https://a.tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png'],
          tileSize: 256,
          attribution: '&copy; OpenStreetMap contributors'
        }
      },
      layers: [
        {
          id: 'background',
          type: 'background',
          paint: { 'background-color': '#f8f4f0' }
        },
        {
          id: 'my-points',
          type: 'symbol',
          source: 'osm',               // dummy source – we’ll add a GeoJSON source later
          layout: {
            // This icon does NOT exist in the style yet → triggers the event
            'icon-image': 'my-missing-icon',
            'icon-size': 1.2,
            'icon-allow-overlap': true
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    center: [0, 0],
    zoom: 2
  });

  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  // 2️⃣  Helper: fetch an image (returns a Promise)
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  function fetchImage(url) {
    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
      map.loadImage(url, (err, img) => {
        if (err) reject(err);
        else resolve(img);
      });
    });
  }

  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  // 3️⃣  Event listener – the core of the solution
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  map.on('styleimagemissing', async (e) => {
    const missingId = e.id;               // e.g. "my-missing-icon"
    console.warn(`🛑 Icon "${missingId}" is missing – trying to load it…`);

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // 3a️⃣  Decide where to look for the image.
    //     You can use any naming convention you like.
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    const baseUrl = 'https://example.com/icons/'; // <-- change to your CDN / folder
    const candidateUrl = `${baseUrl}${missingId}.png`;

    try {
      const img = await fetchImage(candidateUrl);
      map.addImage(missingId, img);
      console.info(`✅ Added "${missingId}" from ${candidateUrl}`);
    } catch (loadErr) {
      // -----------------------------------------------------------------
      // 3b️⃣  Fallback – use a generic placeholder (or generate one on‑the‑fly)
      // -----------------------------------------------------------------
      console.warn(`⚠️ Could not load "${missingId}" from ${candidateUrl}. Using fallback.`);

      // A tiny 1×1 transparent PNG (data‑URI) – you can replace with any placeholder.
      const placeholderDataUri =
        'data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAAEAAAABCAQAAAC1HAwCAAAAC0lEQVR42mP8Xw8AApEB' +
        'B6V6Zc8AAAAASUVORK5CYII=';

      const placeholderImg = await fetchImage(placeholderDataUri);
      map.addImage(missingId, placeholderImg);
      console.info(`✅ Added placeholder for "${missingId}"`);
    }
  });

  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  // 4️⃣  Add a real source + some data so we can see the symbol layer
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  map.on('load', () => {
    map.addSource('my-points', {
      type: 'geojson',
      data: {
        type: 'FeatureCollection',
        features: [
          {
            type: 'Feature',
            geometry: { type: 'Point', coordinates: [0, 0] },
            properties: {}
          }
        ]
      }
    });

    // Re‑assign the source of the symbol layer now that it exists
    map.setLayoutProperty('my-points', 'source', 'my-points');
  });
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

### What the code does

| Step | Explanation |
|------|-------------|
| **1️⃣ Initialise the map** | The style contains a `symbol` layer that references `my-missing-icon`. No image with that id exists yet, so MapLibre will fire `styleimagemissing`. |
| **2️⃣ fetchImage helper** | Wraps `map.loadImage` in a Promise for easier `async/await` usage. |
| **3️⃣ styleimagemissing listener** | The heart of the solution. When the event fires we: <br>• Build a URL based on the missing id.<br>• Try to load the image.<br>• If successful, add it to the style (`map.addImage`).<br>• If the request fails, fall back to a placeholder (transparent PNG in the example). |
| **4️⃣ Add a source & data** | After the map loads we add a tiny GeoJSON source so the symbol layer actually has something to render. The layer’s `source` property is updated to point at the new source. |

