## 1. Why the event exists

When a style JSON contains a `layout.icon-image` (or `layout.pattern`) that refers to an image name that has **not** been added to the map’s style image registry, MapLibre throws a **`styleimagemissing`** event instead of silently failing.  

* The event payload contains the **`id`** (the name the style asked for) and a **`type`** (`icon` or `pattern`).  
* The map will **pause rendering** of any layer that depends on that image until you either add the image or tell it to ignore the request.

That makes it perfect for a “lazy‑load‑on‑demand” workflow or for a graceful fallback when the asset truly does not exist.

