Below is a complete, ready‑to‑copy recipe for dealing with **missing icons** that a MapLibre GL JS style asks for.  
It uses the **MapLibre event system** so you don’t have to edit the style JSON manually – the map will automatically fetch (or generate) the missing image the first time it is needed, and then continue rendering without a “missing‑icon” warning.

---

## 1. The problem in a nutshell

When a style contains a `symbol` layer that references an image that **has not been added to the map’s sprite**, MapLibre throws a warning like:

```
Error: style image "my‑missing‑icon" not found
```

and the symbol is simply not drawn.  
MapLibre (just like Mapbox GL JS) emits a special event called **`styleimagemissing`** every time it encounters such a reference.

> **Key point:** The event payload tells you the *id* of the missing image (`e.id`). You can then load the image (from a URL, a data‑URI, a canvas, etc.) and add it to the map with `map.addImage(e.id, image)`. As soon as the image is added, the map automatically re‑draws the layer that needed it.

---

## 2. Minimal working example

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <title>MapLibre – graceful missing‑icon handling</title>
  <script src="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@4.2.0/dist/maplibre-gl.js"></script>
  <link href="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@4.2.0/dist/maplibre-gl.css" rel="stylesheet" />
  <style>
    body, html { margin:0; height:100%; }
    #map { width:100%; height:100%; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="map"></div>

<script>
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  // 1️⃣  Initialise the map (any style that references a missing icon)
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  const map = new maplibregl.Map({
    container: 'map',
    style: {
      version: 8,
      sources: {
        osm: { type: 'raster', tiles: ['https://a.tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png'], tileSize: 256 }
      },
      layers: [
        { id: 'osm', type: 'raster', source: 'osm' },
        // This layer asks for an icon that does NOT exist yet:
        {
          id: 'my-points',
          type: 'symbol',
          source: {
            type: 'geojson',
            data: {
              type: 'FeatureCollection',
              features: [
                { type: 'Feature', geometry: { type: 'Point', coordinates: [-0.1276, 51.5074] }, properties: {} }
              ]
            }
          },
          layout: {
            'icon-image': 'my-missing-icon',   // <-- missing on purpose
            'icon-size': 1.5,
            'icon-allow-overlap': true
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    center: [-0.1276, 51.5074],
    zoom: 12
  });

  // --------------------------------------------------------------
  // 2️⃣  Listen for the `styleimagemissing` event
  // --------------------------------------------------------------
  map.on('styleimagemissing', async (e) => {
    console.warn(`🛑 Icon "${e.id}" is missing – trying to load it now…`);

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // 3️⃣  Resolve the missing image (you can use any async source you like)
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Example 1 – Load from a remote URL (you could also use fetch + Blob)
    const url = `https://example.com/icons/${e.id}.png`;

    try {
      const img = await loadImage(url);
      // --------------------------------------------------------------
      // 4️⃣  Add the image to the map (synchronously – no callback needed)
      // --------------------------------------------------------------
      map.addImage(e.id, img);
      console.info(`✅ Added "${e.id}" from ${url}`);
    } catch (err) {
      // --------------------------------------------------------------
      // 5️⃣  Fallback: generate a placeholder canvas if the fetch fails
      // --------------------------------------------------------------
      console.warn(`⚠️ Could not load "${e.id}" from ${url}. Using placeholder.`);
      const placeholder = generatePlaceholder(e.id);
      map.addImage(e.id, placeholder);
    }
  });

  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  // Helper: load an image from a URL and return an HTMLImageElement
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  function loadImage(url) {
    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
      const img = new Image();
      img.crossOrigin = 'anonymous'; // needed for cross‑origin URLs
      img.onload = () => resolve(img);
      img.onerror = (e) => reject(e);
      img.src = url;
    });
  }

  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  // Helper: create a tiny canvas with the missing‑icon name drawn on it
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  function generatePlaceholder(id) {
    const size = 64;
    const canvas = document.createElement('canvas');
    canvas.width = canvas.height = size;
    const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');

    // background
    ctx.fillStyle = '#ff6666';
    ctx.fillRect(0, 0, size, size);

    // text (first 2 letters of the id)
    ctx.fillStyle = '#fff';
    ctx.font = 'bold 28px sans-serif';
    ctx.textAlign = 'center';
    ctx.textBaseline = 'middle';
    ctx.fillText(id.slice(0, 2).toUpperCase(), size / 2, size / 2);

    return canvas;
  }

  // --------------------------------------------------------------
  // Optional: log any other map errors (helps debugging)
  // --------------------------------------------------------------
  map.on('error', (e) => console.error('MapLibre error →', e.error));
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

### What the code does

| Step | Explanation |
|------|-------------|
| **1️⃣ Initialise** | Loads a style that deliberately references an image called `my-missing-icon`. |
| **2️⃣ Listen** | `map.on('styleimagemissing', …)` fires *once* for each distinct missing id. |
| **3️⃣ Resolve** | Tries to fetch the image from a predictable URL (`https://example.com/icons/<id>.png`). |
| **4️⃣ Add** | `map.addImage(id, img)` registers the image with the map’s sprite. The layer that triggered the event instantly re‑renders with the newly‑added icon. |
| **5️⃣ Fallback** | If the fetch fails (404, CORS, network), we create a tiny canvas placeholder so the map never shows a blank spot. |
| **Optional error logging** | `map.on('error', …)` catches any other runtime errors (e.g., malformed style). |

---

## 3. Why use the event system instead of pre‑loading everything?

| Reason | Explanation |
|--------|-------------|
| **Lazy loading** | Icons are only fetched when they are actually needed (e.g., a layer becomes visible after a zoom change). |
| **Dynamic styles** | If you let users switch styles at runtime, you don’t have to know ahead of time which icons will be required. |
| **Graceful degradation** | The fallback canvas guarantees that the map never ends up with “invisible” symbols. |
| **Single source of truth** | All missing‑icon handling lives in one place (`styleimagemissing` listener), making the codebase easier to maintain. |

---

## 4. Advanced patterns

### 4.1. Batch‑loading many icons at once

If you know a set of icons may be required (e.g., a catalog of POI types), you can pre‑populate a **cache** and resolve them synchronously:

```js
const iconCache = new Map(); // id → HTMLImageElement or Canvas

async function ensureIcon(id) {
  if (iconCache.has(id)) return iconCache.get(id);

  const url = `/assets/icons/${id}.svg`;
  const img = await loadImage(url);
  iconCache.set(id, img);
  return img;
}

map.on('styleimagemissing', async (e) => {
  try {
    const img = await ensureIcon(e.id);
    map.addImage(e.id, img);
  } catch (_) {
    map.addImage(e.id, generatePlaceholder(e.id));
  }
});
```

### 4.2. Using vector‑tile sprites (PNG + JSON)

If you have a **sprite sheet** (`sprite.png` + `sprite.json`) you can add missing icons from that sheet on‑the‑fly:

```js
let spriteData; // will hold the parsed JSON once fetched

async function loadSprite() {
  const [pngResp, jsonResp] = await Promise.all([
    fetch('/sprites/sprite.png').then(r => r.blob()),
    fetch('/sprites/sprite.json').then(r => r.json())
  ]);
  const img = await createImageBitmap(pngResp);
  spriteData = { img, meta: jsonResp };
}

function getIconFromSprite(id) {
  const meta = spriteData.meta[id];
  if (!meta) return null;

  const canvas = document.createElement('canvas');
  canvas.width = meta.width;
  canvas.height = meta.height;
  const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
  ctx.drawImage(
    spriteData.img,
    meta.x, meta.y, meta.width, meta.height, // source rect
    0, 0, meta.width, meta.height           // dest rect
  );
  return canvas;
}

map.on('styleimagemissing', async (e) => {
  if (!spriteData) await loadSprite();
  const img = getIconFromSprite(e.id);
  if (img) {
    map.addImage(e.id, img);
  } else {
    map.addImage(e.id, generatePlaceholder(e.id));
  }
});
```

### 4.3. React / Vue / Svelte integration

When you’re inside a component framework, you typically set up the listener **once** in a `useEffect`/`onMounted` hook and clean it up on unmount:

```tsx
// React example
useEffect(() => {
  const onMissing = async (e) => { /* same logic as above */ };
  map.on('styleimagemissing', onMissing);
  return () => map.off('styleimagemissing', onMissing);
}, [map]);
```

---

## 5. Full reference of the `styleimagemissing` event

| Property | Type | Description |
|----------|------|-------------|
| `type`   | `"styleimagemissing"` | Event name |
| `id`     | `string` | The **image name** that the style tried to use (e.g., `"my-missing-icon"`). |
| `source` | `any` (usually `null`) | Reserved for future use – currently always `null`. |

> **Note:** The event is **not** emitted for images that are already present in the sprite. It fires **once per missing id** per style load. If you later remove the image with `map.removeImage('my-missing-icon')` and the style still references it, the event will fire again.

---

## 6. Checklist – Did you cover everything?

- [ ] **Listener attached** (`map.on('styleimagemissing', …)`) **before** any layers that might request icons are added (usually right after map creation).  
- [ ] **Async image loading** (`loadImage`) handles CORS (`crossOrigin = 'anonymous'`).  
- [ ] **Fallback placeholder** is provided so the UI never shows a blank symbol.  
- [ ] **Error logging** (`map.on('error', …)`) is in place for debugging.  
- [ ] **Cache** (optional) to avoid re‑downloading the same icon multiple times.  
- [ ] **Cleanup** (`map.off`) if you ever destroy the map instance (important in SPA frameworks).  

---

## 7. TL;DR – One‑liner for quick copy‑paste

```js
map.on('styleimagemissing', async e => {
  try {
    const img = await loadImage(`https://my.cdn/icons/${e.id}.png`);
    map.addImage(e.id, img);
  } catch {
    map.addImage(e.id, generatePlaceholder(e.id));
  }
});
```

Add the two helper functions (`loadImage` and `generatePlaceholder`) from the example above, and you’re done. The map will now **self‑heal** any missing‑icon reference at runtime. Happy mapping!
